### Attribution, Upstream Lineage & Component Licensing Scope

1. **Authorship & Scope of MIT License:**
   * The MIT License above applies to the analytical code, SQL scripts, Jupyter notebook architecture, visualization code, and documentation authored by Mridul Rajgaria within this repository.
   
2. **Attribution to Original Project Concept:**
   * This project builds upon the exploratory analysis workflow, SQL segmentation ideas, and Power BI report structure originally created by **Estefania Marcel** in [tefimarcel/credit-risk-analysis](https://github.com/tefimarcel/credit-risk-analysis).
   * **Licensing Status of Original Repository:** The original repository does not contain an explicit root open-source license file. Under GitHub's Terms of Service and standard copyright law, default copyright is retained by the original author.
   * **Power BI Dashboard Asset:** The binary file (`dashboard/credit_risk_dashboard.pbix`) originates from the public educational work of Estefania Marcel and is preserved here with full attribution for non-commercial educational review and portfolio demonstration. To ensure reproducibility without reliance on third-party binaries, complete independent recreation instructions, DAX formulas, and an automated data pipeline are provided in [`dashboard/README.md`](dashboard/README.md).

3. **Third-Party Dataset Terms:**
   * The underlying loan application data is provided by Home Credit under the [Kaggle Competition Rules and Terms of Use](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/home-credit-default-risk/rules). This repository does not redistribute, relicense, or convey ownership over the raw competition data.
